1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:35,260
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,897
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,117
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real?

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,437
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times!

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,057
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:24,300
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,580
So come aboard and bring along
All your hopes and dreams.

24
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:36,000
Together we will find everything
That we're looking for?

25
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you!

26
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,420
If you wanna be my friend.

27
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,780
We are, we are on a cruise!

28
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are

29
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,420
So, you are alive.

30
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:58,580
The unrivaled pirate captain
who was also the ship's cook.

31
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:00,820
Yes, that's right.

32
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:01,920
I'm still alive.

33
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:04,900
But what has any of
this got to do with you?

34
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,900
I haven't been a pirate
for many years now.

35
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,708
I chose the life of a cook.

36
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,497
Chose the life of a cook, huh?

37
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:16,620
Yeah, right.

38
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,737
You didn't have a choice, old man.

39
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:22,761
You live as a cook because the only
thing you can be now is a cook.

40
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,800
He was known far and wide.

41
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:29,589
Redfoot Seth was a master of deadly
kicks who never used his hands in battle.

42
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:33,217
It was said that with his
mighty legs he could crush

43
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:36,820
bedrock to sand and leave
footprints on solid steel.

44
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,060
Redfoot referred to his boots,

45
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:44,436
which became soaked in the blood of
his enemies as he kicked them down.

46
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:51,940
You know, it really is a pity that you no
longer have that precious leg of yours.

47
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,940
I heard that rumor some time ago.

48
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:59,060
How unlucky for you to have
such an accident at sea.

49
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:04,317
Now that your greatest weapon has been
sacrificed to the sea, you're defenseless,

50
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,988
completely unable to fight.

51
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,540
I don't need to fight anymore.

52
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:13,332
I'm a cook, and as long as I have my
two hands for that, I'll be just fine.

53
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,600
Enough chit-chat.

54
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:15,637
Let's get to the point.

55
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,191
What do you want from me?

56
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,790
Redfoot,

57
00:03:20,873 --> 00:03:22,617
you're the man who sold
the perilous waters

58
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:25,520
of the Grand Line and came back unscathed.

59
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:31,900
There should be a logbook detailing your
tactics, a full year of your journey there.

60
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,280
Give it to me, now!

61
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,630
Whoa!

62
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:40,094
So is he saying you've been
to the Grand Line too, Pops?

63
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:41,930
Yeah.

64
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:42,980
My logbook, huh?

65
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,390
You're right.

66
00:03:44,473 --> 00:03:46,733
I do indeed have a record of my travels.

67
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,940
But I will never hand it over to you.

68
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,440
You ignorant brute.

69
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,880
That logbook is sacred to me.

70
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:57,937
It's the pride of the
crewman that I sailed with.

71
00:03:58,020 --> 00:04:01,020
It's far too important to give to you.

72
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:02,590
Right?

73
00:04:02,673 --> 00:04:03,580
I'll take it.

74
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:07,400
Yes, it's true that
the Grand Line beat me.

75
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,400
Still, I will never give up on it.

76
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:12,177
I am Don Krieg.

77
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:15,120
In the end, it's just another ocean.

78
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:19,180
I had enough weapons,
and men, and ambition.

79
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,397
Regrettably, the only thing
I lacked was information.

80
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,400
I just didn't know enough.

81
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,257
But now I'll fix all that.

82
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:32,937
Once I have your logbook,

83
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:36,844
I'll form another pirate fleet
and seize the legendary One Piece.

84
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:40,940
Then I will stand as ruler
of this great pirate era!

85
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,800
Now hold on!

86
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:50,549
It's me who's gonna be
King of the Pirates!

87
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,160
Huh? Choreboy?

88
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,230
Wait!

89
00:04:54,313 --> 00:04:55,533
Don't be such an idiot!

90
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:58,780
You better back off, Choreboy! No way!

91
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:00,060
Not from this!

92
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,917
Did you say something, kid?

93
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,520
I won't allow that kind of
stupidity again! Oh yeah?

94
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:12,367
Well, stupid or not, I'm just
stating the facts like they are!

95
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,280
This isn't a game.

96
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,120
Yeah, I know.

97
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,734
I'm still gonna conquer the Grand Line.

98
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,360
No, you won't!

99
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:24,177
It's true that we didn't have
the information we needed,

100
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:28,319
but my fleet of 5,000 men was wiped
out in just seven days, you brat!

101
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,720
That sea is hell!

102
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,680
What? One week?

103
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:34,960
Dawn Creek's ships were
wiped out in seven days?

104
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,840
What happened up there?

105
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:41,597
Unfortunately, I don't find your
smart-ass remarks very amusing.

106
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:47,000
If you insist on this foolish behavior,
I'll crush you right here and right now.

107
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,400
Go ahead if you can.

108
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,640
I can and I will.

109
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:58,058
It would be my pleasure to send you
to an early grave, you cocky runt.

110
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,420
What's going on, Luffy?

111
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:06,920
You need a hand?

112
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:09,552
If you don't need help, that's okay, too.

113
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:11,320
Oh, hey, guys.

114
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:14,992
Appreciate the offer, but I
think I can handle this clown.

115
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,330
Oh, too bad.

116
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:20,420
Are those two guys your crew?

117
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,845
That's a pretty small
group you got there, kid.

118
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,320
Well, that's not all.

119
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,660
I got two more.

120
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,500
I'm not a part of your crew.

121
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,940
I'll deal with you later.

122
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:35,054
Right now, I'm going to go feed my men.

123
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,817
Those of you who don't
wish to die can leave

124
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,440
the restaurant now and escape that fate.

125
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:47,980
The only things I'm after are
the logbook and this ship.

126
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:54,257
However if you wish to
stay and be slaughtered I

127
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:57,500
have no problem burying
every last one of you at sea.

128
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,420
Know that.

129
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,720
I'm so sorry, Sanji.

130
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:09,140
I never thought it would be this way.

131
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:12,580
You have nothing to apologize for, sailor.

132
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:18,187
Every cook at this restaurant
did what they thought was right.

133
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,840
That's all there is to
say about that. But boss!

134
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,379
Why are you acting as if
you're taking Sanji's side?

135
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:27,957
This mess is his fault! He's right!

136
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:30,840
Sanji is responsible for
this whole damn thing!

137
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:34,597
Yeah, boss, that man's gonna put your
precious restaurant out of business!

138
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:37,445
You fools don't know what
you're talking about!

139
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:42,140
None of you have any idea what it's
like to be on the brink of starvation.

140
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:45,240
To have no food or
water on the open ocean.

141
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:50,860
There is no way you could possibly understand
what a terrifying prospect that is.

142
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:54,557
It's the most difficult
situation a man could ever face!

143
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,470
What?

144
00:07:55,553 --> 00:07:57,757
I don't know what you're
talking about, Chef Zef.

145
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:00,900
If all you're gonna do is
stand around grumbling,

146
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,880
then leave this place and never come back!

147
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:07,980
I, for one, am gonna stay and fight!

148
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:12,360
I couldn't live with myself if I
accepted defeat! I'm staying, too!

149
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:15,257
After all, this is our
restaurant, isn't it?

150
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:18,281
That's right, and this
place is all I've got, too.

151
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:20,640
What are you doing?

152
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,100
You saw how powerful Dawn is, right?

153
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:28,820
Hey, Ginny, listen up, because
I'm only going to say this once.

154
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:32,358
Feeding someone who's hungry
is my sacred moral duty.

155
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:33,990
But!

156
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,800
Now that your crew is well fed,
I have no obligation to them.

157
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:46,751
With a clean conscience, I can beat
every last one of them to a bloody pulp.

158
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:50,137
If anyone tries to take the
restaurant, they're dead.

159
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:52,867
I'll kill them without
a moment's hesitation.

160
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,430
Got that.

161
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,330
Ha!

162
00:08:57,413 --> 00:08:59,060
You're a real head case, Sanji.

163
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,637
Letting him live, then
threatening to kill him?

164
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:02,800
Can it cook?

165
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,270
See?

166
00:09:04,353 --> 00:09:05,612
This guy's awesome, huh?

167
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,720
Who cares how awesome he is?

168
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:09,919
We gotta get out of here right now!

169
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,159
Easy there, Luffy.

170
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:14,380
It is Don Krieg, but
he's in pretty sad shape.

171
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,460
Hey, Ginny!

172
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,977
You said you didn't know
anything about the Grand Line,

173
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,317
but I thought you'd been there.

174
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,047
That doesn't make any sense.

175
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:27,377
Nothing makes any sense now what
happened to us on the seventh

176
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:31,897
day of our journey through that
cursed sea I don't know if it was a

177
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:37,797
dream or reality I saw things that
I can't bring myself to believe

178
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:41,697
I know in my heart that it's

179
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:46,160
impossible for that entire 50 ship fleet

180
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:51,620
To be completely
eradicated by a single man.

181
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:03,720
It all happened so fast.

182
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:07,040
As soon as this man appeared,

183
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:10,869
he began to systematically sink
our ships one after another.

184
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:17,238
If that raging storm hadn't
come upon us when it did,

185
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:20,929
then that monster would have
destroyed our flagship as well.

186
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:32,120
I don't know if a single
other ship made it out.

187
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,017
It all seems like a terrible
nightmare burned into my memory.

188
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,700
I just want to forget.

189
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:45,600
His eyes, they were like a
hawk's, sharp and murderous.

190
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:49,800
His gaze alone felt like
the cold hand of death.

191
00:10:50,580 --> 00:10:51,410
Huh?

192
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,660
What did he just say?

193
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:03,660
Well then, that can only be
the one known as Hawkeye.

194
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:10,540
Your description of his heartless gaze isn't
proof of his identity in and of itself.

195
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:13,557
But the way he so easily decimated your

196
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:16,620
fleet confirms without
a doubt that it's him!

197
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,380
Hawkeye, Mihawk

198
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:21,840
So you know him, Zoro?

199
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:24,337
Yeah, i do.

200
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:26,840
He's the man i've been looking for.

201
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:33,041
Could that man have had some kind
of score to settle with you guys?

202
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,106
We didn't do anything to him.

203
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,554
Perhaps you disturbed him during a nap.

204
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,040
Stupid cook!

205
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:42,967
Why would he destroy an entire
fleet for something so trivial?

206
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,797
There's no reason to shout.

207
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,220
It's just an example.

208
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:49,857
I thought you might like a little friendly

209
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:53,340
advice on what kind of a
place the Grand Line is.

210
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,720
And what kind of place is that?

211
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:59,140
He probably means that
anything can happen there.

212
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,560
Hey, Luffy, do we really,
really have to go there?

213
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:04,950
Luffy?

214
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:09,880
Hey, Luffy?

215
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,240
That's so awesome!

216
00:12:14,020 --> 00:12:16,100
This is gonna be such a blast!

217
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,653
Do you understand the concept of danger?

218
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:24,140
Finally, my life's goal will be
achieved on the Grand Line. What?

219
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:26,417
My rival.

220
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:29,560
He's out there somewhere,
and I'm gonna find him.

221
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,577
Are you that stupid?

222
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:36,320
It's idiots like you
guys that end up dead.

223
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:40,800
That may be true, but
lay off the name-calling.

224
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:45,920
I devoted my entire life to becoming
the world's greatest swordsman.

225
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:50,820
I made my choice, so I'm the only
one who gets to call me stupid.

226
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:55,340
Hey, what about me?

227
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,640
Me too, right?

228
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,417
I mean, it only seems fair.

229
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,580
Shut up, stupid.

230
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:03,960
What morons.

231
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:08,510
Enough!

232
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:13,060
Do any of you maggots understand
the current situation?

233
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,757
That enormous galleon moored
in front of our dear little

234
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:20,060
restaurant is none other
than Don Creek's flagship.

235
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:24,760
So why don't we check back into
reality and deal with this?

236
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:34,670
Yeah!

237
00:13:34,753 --> 00:13:35,680
We're saved!

238
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:38,660
I can't believe it! We're alive!

239
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,240
It's like a tree!

240
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:41,840
Fire is finally over!

241
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:45,160
We sailed into the pirate
graveyard, but we can't...

242
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,040
Hmm. That's right.

243
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:51,937
And I'm glad you all made it,

244
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:55,667
because I'll need a healthy crew
to go back to the Grand Line.

245
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,820
Hey, why the long faces?

246
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,860
Sir, why are we going back there?

247
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:10,990
Point taken.

248
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:13,680
Are there any other objections?

249
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:28,177
First we need to take over
that floating restaurant.

250
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:31,848
Then we can abandon the wreck
we're on before it falls apart.

251
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:33,940
Don't worry about the enemy.

252
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:36,377
